ed PRs must fill in the \"AI assistance\" section of the PR template, including the responsible human (`@github-id`) — the author-side owner who has read the diff and can explain the changes during review. See [`AI_POLICY.md`](../AI_POLICY.md).","-- Before opening or updating a PR, present the full diff to the responsible human for reading. Do not request review on code no human has read.","+- Before requesting review, present the full diff to the responsible human for reading. Do not request review on code no human has read."," - Hold the automatic Dev CI while iterating on review feedback (e.g., Codex): `gh pr edit <PR> --add-label hold-ci` (applies from the next push; fast checks and review triggers still run; opt-in label workflows such as `ci-cloud` are unaffected)."," - Whenever you add or remove `hold-ci`, say so in your reply to the responsible human: which PR, that heavy CI is paused (so skipped jobs and a failing `ready` check are expected), and that you will remove it once review converges."," - Resume full CI once review converges, without a new commit: `gh pr edit <PR> --remove-label hold-ci`, then re-run the Dev run for the PR head: `gh run rerun $(gh run list -w Dev -c $(gh pr view <PR> --json headRefOid -q .headRefOid) -L1 --json databaseId -q '.[0].databaseId')`."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/meta/app/src/key_with_tenant.rs","lines":["@@ -41,4 +41,16 @@ pub trait KeyWithTenant {","             .push_raw(\"\")","             .done()","     }","+","+    /// Return the encoded directory of the keys of this kind that belong to the tenant.","+    ///","+    /// It is in form of `<__PREFIX>/<tenant>`: the directory a watched cache of these keys takes,","+    /// which holds the keys under `<__PREFIX>/<tenant>/`. Unlike [`Self::tenant_prefix`], it has","+    /// no trailing `/`, which would name the empty-named directory inside it.","+    fn tenant_dir(&self) -> String","+    where Self: kvapi::Key {","+        kvapi::KeyBui